00:44:01.950 --> 00:44:04.050
this year we're over seven billion.

00:44:04.050 --> 00:44:07.170
You know, when you look
back you say, wait a minute.

00:44:07.170 --> 00:44:08.350
- By the way, just for everybody else,

00:44:08.350 --> 00:44:10.963
a million in 1969 was like seven billion.

00:44:10.963 --> 00:44:11.965
- [Rabiah] Right.

00:44:11.965 --> 00:44:13.040
(laughs)

00:44:13.040 --> 00:44:15.285
- No, it's really and privately held.

00:44:15.285 --> 00:44:17.680
I mean that's just,
that's just remarkable.

00:44:17.680 --> 00:44:18.513
- Yeah, and we've laid it out to be

00:44:18.513 --> 00:44:19.910
a privately held family business.

00:44:19.910 --> 00:44:22.170
As my brothers and I say, we're the last

00:44:22.170 --> 00:44:23.140
of the first generation.

00:44:23.140 --> 00:44:24.680
- Educate the kids at home.

00:44:24.680 --> 00:44:26.539
We were talking about
top line revenue numbers.

00:44:26.539 --> 00:44:27.880
- [Steve] Right, yes, top line revenue.

00:44:27.880 --> 00:44:30.830
- So, for example VaynerMedia
this year and the VaynerX

00:44:30.830 --> 00:44:32.970
family 'cause I own some publishing house,

00:44:32.970 --> 00:44:35.590
I'm super proud that we'll be
close to two hundred million.

00:44:35.590 --> 00:44:37.087
- [Steve] Correct.

00:44:37.087 --> 00:44:38.352
