00:45:08.540 --> 00:45:10.221
'cause we can open up another store.

00:45:10.221 --> 00:45:12.709
'Cause there's no way that
you got to this if you didn't,

00:45:12.709 --> 00:45:15.080
in the early days, invest everything back.

00:45:15.080 --> 00:45:16.860
- Yeah, see this is what
I tell the students.

00:45:16.860 --> 00:45:21.280
I sat on the bank board
and on the loan committee,

00:45:21.280 --> 00:45:23.981
and we learned to identify the people

00:45:23.981 --> 00:45:27.330
who were running a lifestyle business.

00:45:27.330 --> 00:45:28.340
They were in a lifestyle business.

00:45:28.340 --> 00:45:29.660
They were not putting it in.

00:45:29.660 --> 00:45:31.390
My brother did not increase

00:45:31.390 --> 00:45:33.200
his lifestyle in those early days.

00:45:33.200 --> 00:45:35.769
Even when we hit that million,
we were pushing vendors

00:45:35.769 --> 00:45:39.532
to put in all the shelving for
free, to put in the equipment

00:45:39.532 --> 00:45:40.740
for free.
- Maximize margins.

00:45:40.740 --> 00:45:42.340
- We were pushing everybody.

00:45:42.340 --> 00:45:43.512
- [Gary] Yep.

00:45:43.512 --> 00:45:44.570
- And we were not buying
buildings or renting 'em

00:45:44.570 --> 00:45:47.697
because our core competency
was running these stores,

00:45:47.697 --> 00:45:48.966
not in real estate.
- Did you ever get

00:45:48.966 --> 00:45:50.382
into real estate?

00:45:50.382 --> 00:45:53.310
- Not, not in a big way.

00:45:53.310 --> 00:45:54.380
- Not heavy in the scale.
- No.

00:45:54.380 --> 00:45:56.020
- Compared to the scale that you are,

00:45:56.020 --> 00:45:57.970
you guys understood your core competency.

00:45:57.970 --> 00:45:59.893
- Yeah, we make money because
we know the damn business.

00:45:59.893 --> 00:46:01.640
We don't know in real estate.
- Look, look.

00:46:01.640 --> 00:46:02.473
Mister, I'll tell you.

00:46:02.473 --> 00:46:04.314
I would argue that not pushing my dad,

00:46:04.314 --> 00:46:06.739
my dad loved the thought of real estate.

00:46:06.739 --> 00:46:09.990
And we spent way too much
money, building this superstore

00:46:09.990 --> 00:46:14.870
in New Jersey that I
intuitively, but I wasn't strong

00:46:14.870 --> 00:46:16.726
enough, so I don't wanna...

00:46:16.726 --> 00:46:18.650
I should have pushed harder to say,

00:46:18.650 --> 00:46:22.170
Dad, we're awesome at running
wine and liquor stores.

00:46:22.170 --> 00:46:24.610
Forget about the ideology of owning,

00:46:24.610 --> 00:46:25.960
of being your own landlord.

00:46:25.960 --> 00:46:27.790
All that money that we
are about to tie up,

00:46:27.790 --> 00:46:30.900
I could've opened up seven
goddamn stores and dominated.

00:46:30.900 --> 00:46:32.140
- [Steve] Exactly.

00:46:32.140 --> 00:46:33.210
- And you understood it.
- That's what we did.

00:46:33.210 --> 00:46:34.043
That's what we did.

00:46:34.043 --> 00:46:34.940
And the bank wouldn't give us money.

00:46:34.940 --> 00:46:36.513
You talk about not making money.

00:46:36.513 --> 00:46:37.511
We didn't make money.

00:46:37.511 --> 00:46:38.344
- There's no VC's like me running

00:46:38.344 --> 00:46:39.850
around writing dumb checks.

00:46:39.850 --> 00:46:40.683
- [Steve] No.

00:46:40.683 --> 00:46:41.853
- Money was tough.

00:46:41.853 --> 00:46:43.402
- Money was so hard.

00:46:43.402 --> 00:46:45.229
We pushed everybody.

00:46:45.229 --> 00:46:46.960
- Back to my question.

00:46:46.960 --> 00:46:49.650
Were the first 10, 15 years
unbelievably dollars back

00:46:49.650 --> 00:46:52.482
into the system, and
was there a transition

00:46:52.482 --> 00:46:56.260
where it became more about maybe
taking a little more profit

00:46:56.260 --> 00:46:58.850
to appreciate some of
the fruits of the labor?

00:46:58.850 --> 00:47:01.070
- The bank wanted us to
open one store a year.

00:47:01.070 --> 00:47:02.090
We were hungry.

00:47:02.090 --> 00:47:03.350
We wanted a store.

00:47:03.350 --> 00:47:06.277
So, I mean, I just kept
asking, how do I get money?

00:47:06.277 --> 00:47:09.910
And in 1972, I found out that they said,

00:47:09.910 --> 00:47:11.933
pay your suppliers slower.

00:47:11.933 --> 00:47:13.530
Pay 'em in 45 days.

00:47:13.530 --> 00:47:16.490
We did, and we went from seven
to 14 stores in one year.

00:47:16.490 --> 00:47:17.680
We almost didn't make it.

00:47:17.680 --> 00:47:19.204
I mean, we were bending.

00:47:19.204 --> 00:47:21.935
We were on bended knees for the bank.

00:47:21.935 --> 00:47:24.460
And fortunately the banker
gave me money, gave us money.

00:47:24.460 --> 00:47:25.860
Or we'd of been in trouble.

00:47:25.860 --> 00:47:29.770
But we went from seven to 14,
really taught us a lesson.

00:47:29.770 --> 00:47:31.650
We almost did not make it through there.

00:47:31.650 --> 00:47:32.577
- [Gary] To number 15.

00:47:32.577 --> 00:47:34.870
- But I always claim I got my master's

00:47:34.870 --> 00:47:37.590
